BRepMesh_FaceChecker (the healer's search for crossing segments of a
face's wires): wires whose boxes are apart are not searched against each
other (mitcad#884).

For each wire, perform() searched every one of its segments in the box
tree of every later wire of the face. On a perforated plate (a plane face
with 1,187 round holes) that is 1,187 x 593 x about 145 tree searches,
nearly all of them rejected at the tree's root: 1.0 s of the plate's
meshing, every time it is meshed. Now a wire's tree is searched only when
the box of all its segments (the root of its own tree) meets the box of
the other wire's segments. A segment's box lies in its wire's box and
both have at least its gap, so a segment of a wire whose box is out of the
other's would be rejected at that tree's root anyway: the crossings found
are the same. The plate's check takes 0.1 s.

Upstream: new.
